  "task": "Write Python 3 function solve(rows). First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 3 equals 0, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 2 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows [day, lifetime] use integer days; day zero is Monday. An item expires at day+lifetime. Move that expiry forward past Saturday/Sunday (remainders 5,6). Return the expiry days in input order.\nReturn the requested value, without printing. Inputs follow the types specified. Do not mutate the input. Standard library is allowed.",
  "specification": "First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 3 equals 0, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 2 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows [day, lifetime] use integer days; day zero is Monday. An item expires at day+lifetime. Move that expiry forward past Saturday/Sunday (remainders 5,6). Return the expiry days in input order.",
  "reference": "def solve(rows):\n out=[]\n for d,n in rows:\n  x=d+n\n  while x%7 in (5,6): x+=1\n  out.append(x)\n return out\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%3!=0 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=2%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
  "mutation": "def solve(rows):\n out=[]\n for d,n in rows:\n  x=d+n\n  while x%7 in (4,5): x+=1\n  out.append(x)\n return out\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%3!=0 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=2%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
